              "In <em>Wilkinson v. Downton (1897)</em>, the defendant played a malicious practical joke on a woman, falsely telling her that her husband had been critically injured in a road accident with both legs broken and was lying at a pub. The shocking statement caused the woman severe nervous shock, leading to prolonged physical illness and permanent psychiatric breakdown.",
