              "Furthermore, in <em>Chairman, Railway Board v. Chandrima Das (2000)</em>, where a foreign national was sexually assaulted by railway employees in a government-run Yatri Niwas at Howrah Station, the Supreme Court rejected sovereign immunity, ruling that public authorities owe an absolute constitutional duty to protect human dignity under Article 21."
