            "citation": "(1799) 8 TR 335",
            "facts": "A minor hired a mare for riding and rode it excessively and carelessly, causing injury to the horse. The owner sued the minor for tort of negligence.",
            "ratio": "The court dismissed the claim. The alleged tort was nothing more than an unperformed term of a contract. A plaintiff cannot convert a breach of contract into a tort to sue an infant."
