            "citation": "(1916) 32 TLR 413",
            "facts": "A father allowed his son to keep an air-gun after being warned of danger. The boy subsequently blinded another child.",
            "ratio": "Parents are liable for their own personal negligence when they fail to exercise reasonable control or entrust lethal articles to minors."
